      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2011-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Simply solving directly: \\[\\begin{aligned} &\\dfrac{2+4+6}{1+3+5} - \\dfrac{1+3+5}{2+4+6} \\\\ &= \\dfrac{12}9 - \\dfrac 9{12} \\\\ &= \\dfrac {16}{12} - \\dfrac 9{12} \\\\ &=\\dfrac 7{12}. \\end{aligned}\\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is C .",
      "hints": [
        "Add the even numbers and odd numbers first",
        "The expression becomes \\(\\frac{12}{9}-\\frac{9}{12}\\)"
      ],
